{"skill":{"slug":"nano-pdf","displayName":"Nano Pdf"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545359433,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":765,"sha256":"4a19c3916062a0b2a303f929be2e11bc89ed8531b47fa565d7936a363f34d4ac","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1839,"sha256":"fa01545214a5004b332babbbd6a14b35a4705e5326d3e839c68b735eb9d9cab1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013577394,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"181524dd56887a2eadc4ec931ad983f4a60e51867fdba38c7f021af961abaa98","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/181524dd56887a2eadc4ec931ad983f4a60e51867fdba38c7f021af961abaa98","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: nano-pdf\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle defines a `nano-pdf` tool, providing instructions for its installation via `uv` from PyPI and usage examples. All actions described involve local execution of the `nano-pdf` CLI for PDF editing. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent in `SKILL.md` or `_meta.json`. The behavior is clearly aligned with the stated purpose and lacks high-risk activities.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159617948},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013577394},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a small, disclosed wrapper for using the nano-pdf CLI to edit PDFs, with the main caveat that it installs an unpinned external package.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Access to local PDF files is expected for a PDF editing CLI, and the artifact tells users to sanity-check the output before sharing it.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The metadata installs the `nano-pdf` CLI via `uv` from an unpinned package name, which is coherent with the skill purpose but leaves normal third-party supply-chain risk.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are narrow and task-focused, with no prompt hijacking, hidden agent directives, credential handling, exfiltration, destructive automation, or unrelated behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact contains no service installation, scheduled task, memory writes, privilege escalation, background worker, or persistence beyond installing the declared CLI dependency.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is editing PDFs with natural-language instructions, and the runtime guidance only shows invoking `nano-pdf edit` on a user-specified PDF page.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, understand that this skill depends on the external `nano-pdf` Python package as resolved by `uv`. Use it on PDFs you are comfortable processing with that CLI, review generated PDFs before distributing them, and prefer a pinned or sandboxed install if your environment handles sensitive documents.","findings":"[T08] expected: The unpinned `nano-pdf` dependency is purpose-aligned because the skill exists to invoke that CLI; this should be treated as supply-chain guidance rather than evidence of malicious or suspicious skill behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013577394}}}}}